        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Buy smart if you will use the classes.</strong> Trainer-led and
            scenic workouts with automatic speed and incline genuinely help some people train
            consistently, and for them the membership is the product. Count it in the price for
            every year you expect to own the machine.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For everyone else, <strong class="text-white">a regular treadmill with better mechanicals
            and Bluetooth output</strong> is usually the better buy: a screen you can upgrade cheaply,
            apps you can switch, and no bill to keep the machine useful. Compare the
            <a href="/best-treadmills-without-subscriptions/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">treadmills that need no subscription</a>
            before deciding.
          </p>
        </div>
